python3: do not probe a non-existent build/ in clean-retain-profile

The host Python build enables PGO (--enable-optimizations), whose
clean-retain-profile target runs four `find build ...` commands. On this
tree the `build/` directory is absent at that point, so:

  - the first three rely on `|| true` for the exit status but still print
    "find: 'build': No such file or directory" to stderr;
  - the fourth is only prefixed with `-`, so make additionally reports
    `make[6]: [Makefile:...: clean-retain-profile] Error 1 (ignored)`.

Guard each `find` with `test -d build`. When the directory exists the
searches run exactly as before; when it does not, nothing is printed and
no ignored error is emitted. Cleanup semantics are unchanged because a
missing build/ has no files to remove.

Applied after 003/009/025, which modify the same Makefile.pre.in.

--- a/Makefile.pre.in
+++ b/Makefile.pre.in
@@ -2971,9 +2971,9 @@
 	find . -name '*.lto' -exec rm -f {} ';'
 	find . -name '*.wasm' -exec rm -f {} ';'
 	find . -name '*.lst' -exec rm -f {} ';'
-	find build -name 'fficonfig.h' -exec rm -f {} ';' || true
-	find build -name '*.py' -exec rm -f {} ';' || true
-	find build -name '*.py[co]' -exec rm -f {} ';' || true
+	-@if test -d build; then find build -name 'fficonfig.h' -exec rm -f {} ';'; fi
+	-@if test -d build; then find build -name '*.py' -exec rm -f {} ';'; fi
+	-@if test -d build; then find build -name '*.py[co]' -exec rm -f {} ';'; fi
 	-rm -f pybuilddir.txt
 	-rm -f _bootstrap_python
 	-rm -f python.html python*.js python.data python*.symbols python*.map
@@ -2982,7 +2982,7 @@
 	-rm -rf Python/deepfreeze
 	-rm -f Python/frozen_modules/*.h
 	-rm -f Python/frozen_modules/MANIFEST
-	-find build -type f -a ! -name '*.gc??' -exec rm -f {} ';'
+	-@if test -d build; then find build -type f -a ! -name '*.gc??' -exec rm -f {} ';'; fi
 	-rm -f Include/pydtrace_probes.h
 	-rm -f profile-gen-stamp
 	-rm -rf iOS/testbed/Python.xcframework/ios-*/bin
